<main class="essay-page">

  <section class="essay-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">The Manifesto</p>
    <h1>Every Bottle<br>Has a Journey</h1>
  </section>

  <article class="essay">
    <p>Pour a glass of wine and you're not just tasting grapes.</p>
    <p class="beat">You're tasting movement.</p>

    <p>Someone had to carry a vine across an ocean for that grape to grow where it grows.</p>
    <p>Someone had to learn a new climate, a new soil, a new way of doing things.</p>
    <p>Somewhere along the way, a technique got borrowed, a name got changed, a tradition got remembered — or forgotten and reinvented by someone who'd never seen the original.</p>

    <p class="pull-quote">That's not a side note in wine's story.<br>That's wine's story.</p>

    <p>We're not used to the wine world saying it that loudly.</p>
    <p>Instead, we're handed a map.</p>
    <p>This region makes this wine.<br>This grape belongs to this country.</p>
    <p class="beat">Except in most cases... it hasn't.</p>

    <p>Regions we think of as timeless are often only a century or two old in their current form. Grapes we associate with one country were sometimes rescued, exported, forgotten, rediscovered, or reinvented by people who came from somewhere else.</p>

    <p>The whole industry — the labor in the vineyards, the styles in the bottle, the way we even talk about taste — has been shaped by people crossing borders, whether by choice or not.</p>

    <p>We explore the world through wine — the migration, the history, the culture, the science, and the farmers, growers, and people behind every bottle.</p>
    <p class="beat">To make it more human.</p>
    <p class="beat">And honestly, more interesting.</p>

    <p>When you understand why a grape ended up where it did, or who built the region you're drinking from, the wine hits different.</p>
    <p class="beat">Literally and figuratively.</p>
    <p>It might mean something else now.</p>

    <p>Understanding that history and celebration can sit at the same table.</p>
    <p>We know that's where wine has always belonged.</p>

    <p>You're not just drinking a Malbec.<br>You're drinking a story about a country that made a French grape its own.</p>

    <p>You're not just drinking Champagne.<br>You're tasting centuries of tradition, science, and identity.</p>

    <p>You're not just opening a bottle.</p>
    <p class="pull-quote">You're opening a journey. A vision. A taste. A movement.</p>

    <p>Wine belongs to everyone.<br>Curiosity is worth more than a score.<br>Every bottle is a small passport.</p>

    <p>We want to take you to the places where people, ideas, and cultures move, mix, and change each other.</p>
    <p class="beat">Glass by glass. Bottle by bottle.</p>

    <p>This is where we start.</p>
    <p class="beat">With a journey. A movement. A people.</p>
  </article>

  <section class="believes-block">
